ue\",\n    \"title\": \"Version 1.3.38-vscode: Config Fixes and Workspace Filtering\",\n    \"description\": \"Continue v1.3.38-vscode includes config.yaml fixes, workspace directory filtering capabilities, and support for .continue/configs directory structure.\",\n    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/releases\",\n    \"date\": \"2026-04-04\",\n    \"community_feedback\": []\n  },\n  {\n    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n    \"title\": \"Copilot SDK Public Preview\",\n    \"description\": \"GitHub Copilot SDK entered public preview, allowing developers to build custom integrations and extend Copilot capabilities.\",\n    \"updateType\": \"announcement\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog\",\n    \"date\": \"2026-04-02\",\n    \"community_feedback\": []\n  },\n  {\n    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n    \"title\": \"Cursor 3: Background Agents in Slack Integration\",\n    \"description\": \"Cursor 3 now supports launching Background Agents directly from Slack by mentioning @Cursor, enabling AI-powered workflows within team communication channels. Also includes BugBot for automatic PR review, one-click MCP server installation, Jupyter notebook support, Memories feature for context persistence, and unified request-based pricing.\",\n    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    \"url\": \"https://cursor.sh/changelog\",\n    \"date\": \"2026-04-01\",\n    \"community_feedback\": [\n      {\n        \"quote\": \"Thirty minutes after the Cursor 3 announcement hit Hacker News, the top comment wasn't about a feature. It was a plea. 'I wish they'd keep the old philosophy of letting the developer drive and the agent assist,' one user wrote. 'I still want to _code_, not vibe my way through tickets.'\",\n        \"source\": \"Medium\",\n        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"productName\": \"Claude Code\",\n    \"title\": \"Week 14 Updates: Computer Use in CLI, Interactive Lessons\",\n 